TITLE:: Arranger
SUMMARY:: Flow of sequence-name labels for the SequencerGui Arrange page.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/PatternChip, Classes/SCViewHolder, Classes/Sequencer, Classes/SequencerGui

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::Arranger:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: that LINK::Classes/SequencerGui:: shows when the Arrange button is pressed. Its view uses a LINK::Classes/FlowLayout:: decorator. Each sequence name is a LINK::Classes/PatternChip:: placed beside the previous label. The chip stores that sequence's id and plays it on the arranger's LINK::Classes/Sequencer::.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates an instance of TELETYPE::Arranger::.

ARGUMENT:: sequencer
The LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: whose sequences this arranger lists and plays.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::Arranger:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: addSequence
Adds a label for CODE::name::. A name that is already shown is left as it is.

ARGUMENT:: name
A LINK::Classes/Symbol::, displayed with CODE::asString::.

PRIVATE:: init
